Place your real `nsfw_v1.tflite` model file in this folder, OR import one
at runtime from inside the app:
  Detection Settings → "Import custom NSFW model (.tflite)"

Loading priority (first-found wins, see TfLiteNsfwClassifier.kt):
  1. filesDir/nsfw_model.tflite   ← user-imported via SAF
  2. assets/nsfw_v1.tflite        ← bundled at build time (CI / manual)
  3. SAFE deterministic fallback  ← keeps the build green when neither exists

Expected format:
  - Input  : float32 [1, H, W, 3], typically 224x224 (BILINEAR resize)
  - Output : float32 [1, 4] softmax over (SAFE, NATURAL, SUGGESTIVE, EXPLICIT)
             OR  [1, 2] softmax over (SFW, NSFW). The classifier auto-detects
             the output dim and maps the NSFW score to severity tiers as:
                 nsfw < 0.40              → SAFE
                 0.40 ≤ nsfw < 0.60       → NATURAL
                 0.60 ≤ nsfw < 0.80       → SUGGESTIVE
                 nsfw ≥ 0.80              → EXPLICIT

When the model file is missing the app falls back to a deterministic SAFE
result. The detection pipeline still ships, but no AI block fires until a
model is provided. UI status text on the AI Settings screen reflects the
live source: "custom imported" / "bundled" / "missing — safe fallback".

Recommended public 2-class quantized MobileNetV2:
  https://huggingface.co/s0md3v/ufal-nsfw-classifier/resolve/main/model.tflite

For 4-class output, train a custom model that matches the spec above. Any
model file that doesn't pass the TFL3 magic-header check OR fails to open
in a throwaway TFLite Interpreter will be rejected by ModelImportManager.
